WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.635
-My first guest
is an Emmy-nominated actor

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:05.605
and comedian who stars
in the new movie --

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:09.008
stars, steals,
whatever you want to say --

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:11.344
the new movie
"Coming 2 America,"

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:15.481
which begins streaming on
Amazon Prime Video this Friday.

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:17.150
Amazon Prime Video, get ready.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.484
It is going to break in half.

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:21.320
Here she is, Leslie Jones!

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.889
Leslie, ah, look at you.

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:24.490
I'm so happy to see you.
-Hey!

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.325
-Hey, buddy.
-Hey, Jimmy!

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:28.094
Hey, New York!

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:31.264
-[ Laughs ]
I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:35.468
I was just talking about you
with Queen Latifah last week.

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.269
Oh, my God. I love her.

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:39.339
-We were talking about
how much we love

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:42.242
when you live-tweet
her show "The Equalizer."

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:43.309
-I love her.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:46.546
-I love anytime
you live-tweet anything.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.981
And, you know, we've --

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:51.784
I've shown clips of "Below
Deck," I think me and you love.

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:53.118
-Oh.
-I showed --

00:00:53.118 --> 00:00:55.355
But, dude, when you were
live-tweeting the news coverage

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:58.892
of the election,
people loved it, especially --

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:01.961
You were commenting
on the guest backgrounds.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:04.163
And --
-It was a accident.

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:07.066
It was a accident.
It happened by accident.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:08.400
I think I was watching it,

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.104
and I was like, "I don't think
these people are aware

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.272
of the stuff
that's behind them."

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:17.009
So I thought that -- You know,
crowd work is my thing.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:19.612
I was like,
"Oh, this is too fun."

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:22.148
And it just became a thing.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:25.484
-We put together some highlights
of your commentaries.

00:01:25.484 --> 00:01:27.219
Check this out.

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:30.056 line:0%
-Yes, Miss Claire
with the black --

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.523 line:0%
I don't think
that's a turtleneck.

00:01:31.523 --> 00:01:33.058 line:0%
That's some kind of ninja suit.

00:01:33.058 --> 00:01:35.394 line:0%
He look like...

00:01:35.394 --> 00:01:37.163 line:0%
like he wake up reading books.

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:38.397 line:0%
We got a clean kitchen?

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:40.399 line:0%
This is where the [bleep]
we doing the news.

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:42.368 line:0%
Rebecca, what do you do
for a living?

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.604 line:0%
If that's New York, bitch,
you paying some money.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:47.941 line:0%
Aah! Steve!

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.575 line:0%
Is he writing on the board?

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:52.278 line:0%
[ Laughing ] I love this dude!

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:56.249
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:58.150
-"He's writing on the board.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:59.651
Ha, ha. I love this dude."

00:01:59.651 --> 00:02:01.086
-Yo, you can't understand

00:02:01.086 --> 00:02:03.856
the love that I felt
for Steve Kornacki.

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:06.559
So, let me explain something,
what was happening.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.728
I was watching
these news channels.

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:11.130
But I didn't like the way
they was covering the election.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.099
They was walking
across the floor

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:15.367
like it was a damn NBA final.

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:16.602
No!

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:20.072
I'm not supposed to see
Wolf Blitzer's shoes!

00:02:20.072 --> 00:02:21.241
No!

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.209
I say no!

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.477
And if they --
And then they was walking

00:02:25.477 --> 00:02:26.913
like they knew everything,

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:29.782
and they wasn't doing nothing
but saying the same thing --

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:31.217
just rubbing they hands

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:33.552
and, like, "Well, what do we got
across here?"

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:36.422
Then take a whole long shot
where they walk across.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:39.024
I wanted to run on there
and punch them in the face,

00:02:39.024 --> 00:02:40.626
like stop!

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:44.263
But then I switched
over to MSNBC,

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:48.635
and there was a nerd
of all calibers.

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:50.436
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:53.906
-He was dressed
for the occasion.

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:55.808
He was stressed out.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:57.943
He was wrinkled.

00:02:57.943 --> 00:03:00.546
He was "dis-shuffled."

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:03.015
He was concerned.

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:07.320
You could tell that that man
had washed up in the wash room.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:10.289
You know how you see them scenes
in the news movies,

00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:11.691
and they'll be like

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:14.359
"Come on, Joyce, you got to
get me the information!"

00:03:14.359 --> 00:03:16.028
That's Steve Kornacki.

00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:17.830
That's Steve Kornacki.
-Yes, yes, yes. He's real.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:21.000
-I knew -- I knew
that something was gon' happen

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.236
when that boy pulled out
that calculator.

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:26.972
I said, "Look here.
Look here!

00:03:26.972 --> 00:03:30.410
I'm gon' find. out.
what's. going. on."

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.111
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:36.014
-Steve Kornacki,
you are my snacky.

00:03:36.014 --> 00:03:37.583
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:40.186
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.356
-I --

00:03:44.356 --> 00:03:46.025
I heard that you got mad at him

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.359
when he was
going on other things.

00:03:47.359 --> 00:03:49.361
He was doing other stuff.
You go, "Stop it."

00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:52.030
They're taking him from you.
-Wha--

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:55.735
Why is you passing Steve around
like a joint?

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.937
He's not a joint.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:02.041
He is a valuable "statician."

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.876
It's just, you can't be
putting him on --

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:05.944
He doing football stats.

00:04:05.944 --> 00:04:08.581
I bet you
Steve was dying inside,

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:12.051
using them numbers
for that mess!

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:15.454
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:17.323
I want to talk to you --

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:21.794
I want to talk to you about
"Coming 2 America," the sequel.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.162
-"Coming 2."

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.329
-Leslie, let me
tell you something.

00:04:24.329 --> 00:04:25.931
I have known you for years now.

00:04:25.931 --> 00:04:27.800
I've seen you destroy.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.736
I've seen -- I've worked
with you in sketches.

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:33.906
I've seen you on-stage.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:36.509
You're already
in legendary status.

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:38.711
-Aww, that's so sweet.
-This movie put you

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.646
in a whole new thing

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:42.448
that I don't even know
if you're ready for this thing,

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:45.218
'cause honestly,
it was laugh-out-loud,

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:46.886
screaming-laughing funny for me.

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.955
I go, "What is going on?
They let her be --

00:04:49.955 --> 00:04:52.258
They let her
just go off and play."

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:53.459
We've had Eddie on.

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:55.060
We've had everyone
from the movie on,

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.562
and they all bring it up.

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:58.264
I bring --
I'm about to bring it up.

00:04:58.264 --> 00:04:59.699
They're like,
"No, no, stop. Leslie."

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:01.167
I go, "Yes."

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:04.603
So, basically, am I allowed to
say who you play in the movie?

00:05:04.603 --> 00:05:05.904
'Cause I'm not sure
what I can --

00:05:05.904 --> 00:05:08.141
-I think so. I'm his baby mama.

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:10.209
-There you go. So, he has a son.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:13.645
-Basically. Basically.
-The Prince has a son.

00:05:13.645 --> 00:05:15.181
-The Prince has a son.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.549
-Wow.
-By a real chick,

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:17.883
like one of them real chicks.

00:05:17.883 --> 00:05:19.685
Like, yeah. You know?

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:23.823
Shari wasn't the only one
he hit in Queens, you know?

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:26.659
-How was Eddie
to do the scenes with?

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:28.027
Was he fun?

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:31.897
-It was funny, because every
time he would walk on-set,

00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:35.568
it's just very surreal,
because you know I'm a comedian.

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.870
And Eddie is who, you know,

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:41.073
like, after Richard Pryor,
I was like, "Oh, my God.

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:43.276
There's a guy who can perform
like Richard Pryor."

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:45.278
That's literally
what I thought of Eddie Murphy

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:47.613
when I first saw him.
I was like, "Oh, my God.

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:49.782
There's somebody
as funny as Richard Pryor?"

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:51.484
-Yeah.
-And just to be on a set

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:54.120
with somebody like that,
and he's just, like, Eddie,

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.721
you know?
He's just walking through,

00:05:55.721 --> 00:05:59.958
and you're like, "Yeah. Yeah.
I honestly love you."

00:05:59.958 --> 00:06:03.229
-Do you remember the first time
when he laughed at you?

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:04.697
Laughed with you?

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:07.066
-Actually, Eddie saw me
at the Laugh Factory

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:10.102
long, long, long
before "SNL" and all of that.

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:11.371
-Really?

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:13.773
-So, he saw me
at the Laugh Factory.

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:16.575
And Pooky, the dude
that was running the room --

00:06:16.575 --> 00:06:18.811
There's always a dude
named Pooky running the room.

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:21.280
And he said, "Hey,
Eddie wants to meet you."

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.882
And I went over to the side,

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:24.917
and I was like,
"Oh, my God. Eddie Murphy."

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:26.551
And he was like,
"Oh, my God. You were so funny."

00:06:26.551 --> 00:06:27.753
And I said, "Eddie --"

00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:29.655
I think -- I asked him
the dumbest question.

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:33.659
I was like, "Eddie, if you was
a comic like in this time,

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:36.228
would you do BET ComicView?"

00:06:36.228 --> 00:06:38.231
And he was like, "Yeah.

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:39.298
Definitely."

00:06:39.298 --> 00:06:41.667
[ Laughs ]
And I was like, "Okay."

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.002
-Wow.
-And I was like --

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:45.338
I went home, and I was like,

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:47.873
"Anything. You could have
asked him anything!

00:06:47.873 --> 00:06:50.542
And that's what you asked him?"
It was --

00:06:50.542 --> 00:06:53.078
And then I got to see him again,
you know, through "SNL"

00:06:53.078 --> 00:06:54.613
and all of that.
But, you know --

00:06:54.613 --> 00:06:55.847
-This is going to --

00:06:55.847 --> 00:06:58.151
Seriously, I think
it's going to break Amazon.

00:06:58.151 --> 00:07:00.819
They better be ready for this,
'cause it's happening on Friday.

00:07:00.819 --> 00:07:02.388
-I hope so.
-Everyone in the world

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:03.688
is talking about this movie.

00:07:03.688 --> 00:07:05.123
I want to show a clip.

00:07:05.123 --> 00:07:08.494
Here's the great Leslie Jones
in "Coming 2 America."

00:07:08.494 --> 00:07:09.895
Take a look at this.

00:07:09.895 --> 00:07:13.132
-[ Laughing ] Ooh! What?!

00:07:13.132 --> 00:07:14.466
-Hashtag family.

00:07:14.466 --> 00:07:16.102
-That's the last surprise.

00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:17.269
-Hey! What's up, y'all?

00:07:17.269 --> 00:07:20.106
-Hi. What's up, fam?

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:21.707
I'm gon' hug you
'cause I'm a hugger.

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:23.676
Hey, Queen.

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:26.078
I'm sorry I slept with your man.

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:28.513
-What is going on here?
-Oh, children.

00:07:28.513 --> 00:07:31.784
Children, I would love
for you to meet your brother.

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:34.053
-And my name is Mary.
How you doing?

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:35.921
Just call me your second mom.

00:07:35.921 --> 00:07:38.824
-But you really
don't have to, girls.

00:07:38.824 --> 00:07:41.828
-I mean, but you should, though,
'cause I kind of am.

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:46.165
-Well, look at us, just one
big, happy, Zamundan-American,

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:47.733
aristocratic blended family.

00:07:47.733 --> 00:07:51.137
-Ah, just like the Kardashians!
[ Chuckles ]

00:07:51.137 --> 00:07:53.939
-Leslie Jones!
"Coming 2 America"

00:07:53.939 --> 00:07:57.076
will be streaming on
Amazon Prime Video this Friday.

